00:05:01.889 --> 00:05:03.758
As we are filming this right now,

00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:04.998
so for everybody who's listening,

00:05:04.998 --> 00:05:07.598
I'm gonna have DRock
show Staphon right now,

00:05:07.598 --> 00:05:09.813
who's actually filming us and Meerkatting.

00:05:09.813 --> 00:05:12.820
Staphon, flip over the screen,

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.847
show the camera, flip over your screen.

00:05:15.847 --> 00:05:19.016
Zoom in DRock, no, no,
flip, don't look at you.

00:05:19.016 --> 00:05:21.353
Show the, there we go, thank you.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:24.177
Yeah, so you know, right now we are,

00:05:24.177 --> 00:05:27.651
we're Meerkatting, I don't
know if you know that,

00:05:27.651 --> 00:05:29.911
but that's an actual animal,
you can go back to me.

00:05:32.993 --> 00:05:35.390
I think if I was Meerkat,
I'd be very concerned.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.068
You know, obviously we're all
enjoying the Kat quite a bit,

00:05:39.068 --> 00:05:40.368
live streaming, phone to phone,

00:05:40.368 --> 00:05:43.492
peer to peer is clearly here,

00:05:45.152 --> 00:05:49.419
but if I was Meerkat, I would be concerned

00:05:49.419 --> 00:05:52.812
about this acquisition because clearly

00:05:52.812 --> 00:05:54.417
if it's got the same functionality,

00:05:54.417 --> 00:05:56.083
which is what it's rumored to have,

00:05:56.083 --> 00:05:59.008
I haven't seen it yet, but
I will probably test it out

00:05:59.008 --> 00:06:01.243
this weekend if I get a chance,

00:06:01.243 --> 00:06:02.218
at South by Southwest.

00:06:02.218 --> 00:06:03.967
Oh, which reminds me, if you're
goin' to South by Southwest,

00:06:03.967 --> 00:06:05.915
please check out my talk, Saturday

00:06:05.915 --> 00:06:09.532
at three PM, Austin time.

00:06:10.682 --> 00:06:12.824
I think that I'd be concerned,

00:06:12.824 --> 00:06:13.717
and I think that I'm definitely

00:06:13.717 --> 00:06:15.363
gonna check it out because I should,

00:06:15.363 --> 00:06:16.481
and because it's gonna be integrated

00:06:16.481 --> 00:06:20.259
probably natively into the Twitter app.

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:23.774
So, it will be interesting
to see this play out

00:06:23.774 --> 00:06:26.009
if it's gonna be a fast move

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:28.427
by Twitter to integrate.

00:06:28.427 --> 00:06:29.646
We've seen this before, you know,

00:06:29.646 --> 00:06:32.998
I remember people saying, "Oh
Facebook's doing check ins,

00:06:32.998 --> 00:06:34.116
"Foursquare's dead."

00:06:34.116 --> 00:06:35.314
And it didn't happen because it wasn't

00:06:35.314 --> 00:06:37.305
native to the product, but I do think

00:06:37.305 --> 00:06:39.337
this functionality clearly,
cause Meerkat's built

00:06:39.337 --> 00:06:41.287
on top of Twitter, from the sign in,

00:06:41.287 --> 00:06:42.811
from the push outs, from the engagement,

00:06:42.811 --> 00:06:44.030
when people are commenting right now,

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.676
it's showing up on Twitter.

00:06:45.676 --> 00:06:47.789
This is deeply integrated into Twitter,

00:06:47.789 --> 00:06:51.811
and thus will be interesting
to watch what happens here.

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:54.879
I absolutely plan on using it.

00:06:54.879 --> 00:06:58.496
I see a scenario where
this is really detrimental

00:06:58.496 --> 00:07:00.731
to Meerkat, I see a scenario where

00:07:00.731 --> 00:07:02.498
Twitter tries to see if both can survive.

00:07:02.498 --> 00:07:04.022
I don't know, it'll be
interesting to watch,

00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:06.988
but the acquisition has
definitely caught my attention.

00:07:06.988 --> 00:07:08.959
I'm paying very close attention,

00:07:08.959 --> 00:07:12.393
and I plan on testing out the product

00:07:12.393 --> 00:07:14.262
as soon as possible so I can make

00:07:14.262 --> 00:07:15.873
my judgements on differences.

00:07:16.781 --> 00:07:18.854
- [Voiceover] Samantha asks,
"How do your right hooks

00:07:18.854 --> 00:07:21.562
"differ for a free service
versus a paid one?"

00:07:23.628 --> 00:07:25.620
- When you're throw the
right hook that's free

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.830
I get excited because
there's less friction,

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.106
and it feels like I'm gonna really be able

00:07:31.106 --> 00:07:32.770
to land that right hook.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:36.307
The problem is, there's a
really funny thing about free.

00:07:36.307 --> 00:07:38.947
Free creates a scenario where people value

00:07:38.947 --> 00:07:40.938
it for what it's been put out.

00:07:40.938 --> 00:07:42.585
It's really interesting.

00:07:42.585 --> 00:07:43.985
I think that a lot of people who watch

00:07:43.985 --> 00:07:46.322
this show value it quite a bit.

00:07:46.322 --> 00:07:49.390
I think that the 10% left,
if I started charging

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:52.031
four bucks an episode,
or two bucks an episode,

00:07:52.031 --> 00:07:53.453
the you know, actually you know what,

00:07:53.453 --> 00:07:54.814
that's gonna be the question of the day.

00:07:54.814 --> 00:07:56.013
And I know this is a tough question,

00:07:56.013 --> 00:07:57.801
and by the way, I will
not be charging for this,

00:07:57.801 --> 00:08:00.057
so don't worry, don't hedge and say zero,

00:08:00.057 --> 00:08:01.438
I don't have any plans on it.

00:08:01.438 --> 00:08:04.506
But if I was, what would you pay

00:08:04.506 --> 00:08:07.066
to watch an episode of
The #AskGaryVee Show?

00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:09.544
And yeah that's the real question.

00:08:09.544 --> 00:08:12.551
And clearly, I expect most
of the comments to be zero,

00:08:12.551 --> 00:08:14.136
or no, because I respect that there's

00:08:14.136 --> 00:08:16.291
so much content out
there, but I do believe

00:08:16.291 --> 00:08:20.455
that my content is better
than a substantial amount

00:08:20.455 --> 00:08:22.405
of content out there in the world.

00:08:22.405 --> 00:08:23.828
Especially when it talks about

00:08:23.828 --> 00:08:26.753
new platforms, business,
running businesses,

00:08:26.753 --> 00:08:29.943
leadership, entrepreneurship,
start up, tech culture.

00:08:29.943 --> 00:08:32.462
So, I do think that we'll
see a surprising number,

00:08:32.462 --> 00:08:33.395
and I'm sure you're
probably getting answers

00:08:33.395 --> 00:08:35.489
right now in Meerkat,
so Staphon, feel free

00:08:35.489 --> 00:08:39.269
to not shout it out, cause
I want to be surprised.

00:08:39.269 --> 00:08:42.722
But I do think that
it's really funny to me

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.611
to think about the 10% of
you that I would expect

00:08:44.611 --> 00:08:47.396
to pay for it that if you
were paying four bucks for it

00:08:47.396 --> 00:08:49.406
you'd actually value the show more.

00:08:49.406 --> 00:08:51.642
It's really quite interesting psychology.

00:08:51.642 --> 00:08:53.815
So, how do I act differently?

00:08:53.815 --> 00:08:56.091
One, when I throw right
hooks, for example,

00:08:56.091 --> 00:08:59.077
when I tweet out later
today that episode 80 is up.

00:08:59.077 --> 00:09:01.840
You know, I expect to
land more than saying,

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.294
"Episode 80 is up, pay
me three dollars Snapcash

00:09:05.294 --> 00:09:06.494
"if you want to watch it."

00:09:06.494 --> 00:09:09.459
You know, I have a little less angst

00:09:09.459 --> 00:09:10.719
of the conversion because I know

00:09:10.719 --> 00:09:12.222
that there's no friction financially,

00:09:12.222 --> 00:09:17.140
which is one, besides time,
finance is the friction.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:21.772
And so, I think it's got a
totally different cadence,

00:09:21.772 --> 00:09:24.596
different expectation,
different pressure hold.

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:25.841
I think it's easier.

00:09:26.322 --> 00:09:28.374
- Hey Gary, answer my question.

00:09:28.374 --> 00:09:30.812
By the way, go Giants.

